Simulator::Cell::SoftBodyStep=0x00E5A430 ; verified cdecl void(cell*, resData*, float dt), plain ret (caller UpdateCells E7CA72 pushes 3, add esp,0xC; sets ESI = cell itself before calling E5A1A0). Shape matching of a soft body (+0x248 GFX set, +0x250 particles > 1): FUN_00E85D70 fits a rotation from the particle positions (parts+4+12k) to the rest shape (0x16AD6C0 + type(+0x24C)*0x300), writes +0x5C (flag 2, counter++) and +0x24 (same matrix, blend arg 0), the angular speed to +0x1D0 and goal offsets (goal - pos) to parts+0x11944+12k. Row-vector convention: goal = rest * M + centre, so yaw = atan2(M[1], M[0]). n == 1: copies a constant 3x3 to +0x24 and returns (+0x5C untouched). GOG 2016: likely 0xE5A450 (neighbours moved by -0x20), not ported (frozen build)
Simulator::Cell::SpawnLoot=0x00E771D0 ; verified (Ghidra 2026-10-24, GOG 2024: plain ret at E7752E/E77799, query read as arg 3, loot table as arg 7) cdecl void(ref* res, ResourceKey* model, query*, const Vec3* pos, float size, int level, ref* lootTable, float dt, u32* outIdx, int* outCount): picks one entry of the loot table by weight (type 1: RandomInt(+0x14)+(+0x10) cells of entry +4 via E76480 with an outward velocity, type 2: repeat, 0: nothing). Callers: KillCell (level within the player's level .. +1, loot level = victim level - 1), event 5 E7ADD0 (break), DestroyCell(idx, 1) (when the level is not the player's - 1), E77AC0, E791F0
